    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0576" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1360</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi>
                        </placeName> [<date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1917-05-23T15:00:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1917-05-21T00:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date><hi rendition="#italic">; received May 23, 1917,
                            3 a.m</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reports from all over country show orderly celebration 20th May. Apprehension in
                    Habana kept people indoors till afternoon when immense crowds joined in
                    celebrating inauguration. No disorders or bad feelings. Today liberals of
                    consequence called at Palace and congratulated President. No activity by
                    insurgents or bandits anywhere today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
